# autotao autonomous loop — durable system-cron version.
# NOT INSTALLED as of 2026-07-24: the operator prefers the foreground supervision
# console (scripts/autotao.sh in tmux, automation.autoLaunch) as the sole
# maintainer of runs — it shows live progress and does the same gated
# launches. Keep this file only as the fallback recipe if the console stops
# being used.
# Install by appending to your crontab (preserves existing entries):
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; grep -v '^#' /path/to/autotao/scripts/crontab.example) | crontab -
# Budgets are NOT set here any more. These lines used to carry their own copy
# (`should-run.sh 80 97 15`) — a fourth independent set of ceilings, weekly 97
# against the console's 90 — which is the drift that killed three runs on
# 2026-07-26. should-run.sh now REJECTS positional budget args; edit
# scripts/budgets.conf, which every caller reads.
#
# Launch only via scripts/launch.sh: it runs the gate and the watchdog preflight
# synchronously, detaches the run itself, and returns a real exit code
# (0 launched · 1 usage · 2 memory · 3 unknown · 4 already running).
41 0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21 * * * cd /path/to/autotao && bash scripts/launch.sh
41 5,11,17,23 * * * cd /path/to/autotao && bash scripts/should-run.sh && bash scripts/run-once.sh codex
# Tiered babysitter (scripts/supervisor-tick.sh): free bash health checks every 15
# min; spawns haiku to settle a finished run's books, fable/opus only on real
# breakage (crash streaks, hung runs). Safe alongside the launch lines above.
*/15 * * * * cd /path/to/autotao && bash scripts/supervisor-tick.sh
